& [Question]
  + determine which source-preserved ReverberantAttentionTrace concepts already have exact provider-free Cantor substrates and which require new canonical semantics
  + preserve reuse candidates by identity without importing broader authority from their original features

& [ExactAttentionFrameSubstrate]
  + SharedAttentionFrame already binds generation predecessor digest purpose policy participants propositions constraints pinned SOP anchors evidence current focus byte accounts applied deltas applied compactions attestations status semantic digest and frame digest
  + AttentionCompaction already binds an actor policy exact base generation and digest retained focus byte reductions rationale evidence and a receipt naming released focus and headroom change
  + compaction refuses stale base duplicate identity unauthorized faculty missing rationale missing evidence non-subset retention capacity increase no-op and insufficient-headroom outcomes
  + this is reusable structural evidence for explicit release and retention but not authority to reinterpret compaction as elapsed-time or semantic-event decay

& [ExactLedgerAndReentrySubstrate]
  + AttentionLedger is a pure content-addressed append-only map of validated frames sessions and events with a root digest
  + every session state binds sequence exact head generation digest status event refs and a session digest; apply uses compare-and-set ledger sequence and head coordinates
  + AttentionContinuation is already a compact exact locator while full frames and events remain readable
  + the local ledger server is deliberately volatile and process restart loses unpersisted sessions
  + compact reflection-loop AttentionReentryFrame already commits to a retained replay-valid prefix and declares exact prefix under host custody while refusing hidden-state semantic-equivalence and provider claims
  + DispatchLifecycleCheckpoint already binds serialized value state next operation and exact resume comparison; twelve fixture cases prove equality with uninterrupted traces
  + compact host-custody handles and an immutable in-memory custody map already prove exact lookup-to-resume with an observed 83.12-percent aggregate byte reduction in the governed fixture

& [ExactSemanticEventSubstrate]
  + SemanticTraceEvent already binds event identity logical index kind procedure process subject generation normalized payload digest and causal predecessor refs
  + SemanticState already carries purpose focus inside boundary outside frontier evidence uncertainty budget pending effects and status
  + yielded-state reentry already refuses any restored state that is not the exact current yielded state
  + HistoryReviewEvent already records current subject purpose operation candidate count selected records counterevidence exclusions coverage projection reconciliation and transition decision
  + SucceedingSopProposal already conserves an explicit unresolved frontier across proposal and review admission
  + these forms support causal event accounting anchor input and public rationale but do not yet define a complete cross-feature ReverberantEvent ledger

& [ExactAnchorSubstrate]
  + SharedAttentionFrame separates pinned SOP anchors from removable current focus and assigns pinned-anchor bytes a non-removable account during compaction
  + SemanticAnchorCatalogue already provides exact identity label applicability typed-relation lexical embedding and learned-route channels with retained excluded contradicted stale incompatible and clipped contribution statuses
  + SemanticAnchor curator verification already requires an externally governed exact identity selection source anchor rationale policy binding and signature while denying semantic truth and effect authority
  + this is reusable input for governing-anchor resolution and term candidates but does not yet produce the proposed anchored drifted or underdetermined reconstruction disposition

& [NewSemanticsRequired]
  + TraceItem needs an exact subject source role scope transform completion invalidation restoration-pointer salience floor and lifecycle form
  + DecayPolicy needs a deterministic admitted clock or semantic-event basis bounded score rule mandatory retention floors refresh evidence release conditions and stable tie breaking
  + DecayReceipt and RefreshReceipt must account every before and after score floor refresh release and reason without rewriting prior events
  + RestorationCheckpoint must bind exactly which existing ledger frame procedure trace reentry prefix frontier and evidence identities are sufficient for one declared recovery scope
  + ReconstructionProposal must remain separate from admitted state and expose every supplied checkpoint item omitted item proposed synthesis and uncertainty
  + AnchorCheck must return exactly anchored drifted or underdetermined and conserve mandatory anchors denials open requirements latest accepted receipts and unresolved frontier
  + NarrativeProjection must render only admitted semantic events public rationales and cited interpretations and must never claim hidden token-level chain of thought

& [ReuseDecision]
  + reuse exact ContentDigest SemanticId causal predecessor strict JSON bounded collections and self-excluding digest practices
  + adapt SharedAttentionFrame anchor focus and capacity separation AttentionCompaction retention accounting AttentionLedger compare-and-set history compact checkpoint custody SemanticTrace causality HistoryReview reconciliation semantic-anchor source binding and unresolved-frontier conservation
  + do not merge their authority domains or mutate existing profiles in P0; form one new pure adapter layer over supplied values
  + keep durable persistence model-assisted reconstruction host projection provider execution and autonomous continuation outside the first provider-free formation

& [SmallestFormationCandidate]
  + RAT-P0 is a pure trace-policy compiler decay transition evaluator reconstruction-form validator and anchor verifier over supplied bounded fixtures
  + first fixtures use synthetic exact checkpoints and semantic events only and perform no clock filesystem environment process network model provider MCP Git workspace or persistence operation
  + NarrativeProjection formation may define a deterministic event-to-public-record mapping but implementation should remain a later sub-slice unless its schema is necessary to prove trace lifecycle completeness

& [FormationQuestions]
  + select semantic-event count versus supplied logical time as the first decay basis
  + decide whether mandatory floors attach to trace-item role source requirement identity or all three
  + define checkpoint sufficiency without pretending a digest reproduces omitted bytes
  + define conflict precedence among source authority latest accepted receipt and unresolved-frontier records
  + define when an underdetermined state may request retrieval and when it must stop for operator judgment
  + define narrative redaction sensitivity retention and interpretation labels before any human-facing projection

& [Disposition]
  + substrate_audit_complete_formation_not_started
  + no existing component alone implements reverberant decay faithful reconstruction anchor triage or narrative projection
  + no canonical schema satisfaction signature implementation provider use durable state or effect authority is inferred
